WEBVTT

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.220
﻿He's set his sword to the same
﻿particle band as my beam!

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:33.390
<i>﻿That's right.</i>

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:37.820
﻿This sword has a particle
﻿alteration coating.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.990
<i>﻿It changes the particle band
﻿based on the blade direction,</i>

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.700
<i>﻿and cuts through the beams.</i>

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.440
﻿When you match it to the field's
﻿control particle band,

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.280
<i>﻿this is what happens.</i>

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:16.600
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:23.470
﻿What an amazing Gunpla!
﻿How did he build it?

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:26.370
﻿I can't wait to battle him.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:28.270
﻿Yeah!

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.710
﻿Now I've advanced to the best 8.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:36.380
﻿My next opponent is...

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.290
﻿Nils Nielsen.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.490
﻿Can I have a moment with you?

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.890
﻿Just as I planned.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.590
﻿I'll get straight to the point.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:28.330
﻿We at PPSE are fully prepared
﻿to be your personal sponsor.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:31.760
﻿Materials for building Gunpla,
﻿a state-of-the-art workshop,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.570
﻿and an excellent support team.

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.330
﻿We'd provide them free of—

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:38.170
﻿Wait a second.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.640
﻿I already have
﻿Yajima Trading sponsoring me.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:49.510
﻿Plus, shouldn't you be backing
﻿Meijin Kawaguchi of your works team?

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:53.750
﻿To spread Gunpla Battle further,

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.960
﻿Chairman Mashita wishes to support
﻿excellent players more widely.

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:04.330
﻿If you accept our sponsorship,
﻿we don't ask anything in return.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:07.400
﻿And we won't cause you trouble.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.330
﻿Nothing in return?

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:14.070
﻿Why are they so eager
﻿to get me on their side?

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.810
﻿What do you think?

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:20.110
﻿I'm honored that you
﻿think so highly of me.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.610
﻿Well...

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.520
﻿I'd gladly accept your sponsorship.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:26.650
﻿Thank you.

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:29.690
﻿Chairman Mashita
﻿will be delighted to hear that.

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.760
﻿I'll show you to our workshop at—

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.430
﻿No, there's no need for that.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:41.300
﻿My Sengoku Astray is so perfect
﻿that there's no need to add anything.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:46.840
﻿But there is one thing
﻿I'd like to request of PPSE.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:47.840
﻿What is it?

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.010
﻿The factory that produces...

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.010
﻿the Gunpla battle system,
﻿or the Plavsky particle generator.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.250
﻿May I please see it?

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.450
﻿The factory?

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:05.620
﻿If I understand
﻿the particle's manufacturing process,

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:09.360
﻿the matching of my Gunpla and the
﻿Plavsky particles will improve vastly.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:13.860
﻿I can't think of any better way
﻿to strengthen my machine.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:15.770
﻿I see.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:19.740
﻿That's why he accepted our sponsorship.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.610
﻿So what'll you do?

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:28.210
Alright.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:31.480
﻿I'll talk to our management to see
﻿if I can get you permission.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.850
﻿Thank you.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:38.620
﻿But it might take some time
﻿before we can get you permission.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.060
﻿Why don't we wait until
﻿the quarterfinals are over?

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:47.230
﻿Okay. Then if I get permission...

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.900
﻿We'll contact you straight away.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.240
﻿Nils Nielsen.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:02.750
﻿That's why this scientific genius
﻿suddenly entered the tournament.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:05.920
To find out the secret of
﻿the Plavsky particle.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.220
﻿But you see, little boy.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.850
﻿That thing...

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:11.320
﻿That place is off limits.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:18.660
﻿The factory tour will be
﻿after the quarterfinals, huh.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:21.030
﻿That's a very restrictive condition.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.500
﻿There must be a reason.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.340
﻿I'm... I'm scared, Baker.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:32.610
﻿Don't worry anymore, Chairman.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:35.510
﻿I-I mean, that boy...

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:38.350
﻿It seems he doesn't remember for now,

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:40.480
﻿but he could recall everything.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:42.250
﻿Recall what?

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:45.760
﻿My secret.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.960
﻿And that of the Plavsky particle—

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.560
﻿Chairman Mashita said back then,

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:57.270
﻿that the boy might recall the secret
﻿of him and the Plavsky particle.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:00.200
﻿The boy the Chairman fears.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:03.770
﻿And why does my factory tour
﻿have to be after the quarterfinals?

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:06.810
﻿Deducing from the situation,

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:11.850
﻿the boy must be my next opponent.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:15.790
﻿Sei Iori or Reiji.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.690
﻿One of those two must know the secret.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.900
﻿If my deduction is correct, PPSE...

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:30.200
﻿no, Chairman Mashita wants to
﻿get them out of the tournament

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.800
﻿before either of them recalls the secret.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:35.870
﻿And that's why they approached me.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:38.710
﻿So, even if I defeat them,

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.350
﻿I should assume I won't
﻿get a factory tour.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.650
﻿It's just a verbal promise.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:47.080
﻿They can make up
﻿any reason to call it off...

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:47.820
﻿Huh?

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:52.920
﻿Ow. Ow. I give up!

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:55.230
﻿M-Miss Caroline? Sorry about that!

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.700
﻿You really are
﻿a master of martial arts.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.600
﻿I just have a bit of
﻿experience in Aikido.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.530
﻿Anyway, What're you doing here?

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:07.500
﻿You're saying I can't cheer
﻿for my boyfriend?

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:11.440
﻿Huh?

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:12.710
﻿Boyfriend!?

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.340
﻿Am I the boyfriend!?

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:15.910
﻿Of course.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:18.920
﻿You accepted my dad's
﻿company's sponsorship.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:22.090
﻿My dad's things are my things.
﻿Meaning...

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:27.560
﻿You're mine, too!

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:30.160
﻿That formula is incorrect!

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.000
﻿It doesn't follow reason or logic!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.770
﻿I'm not good enough for you?

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.470
﻿Not good enough!?

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:43.110
﻿N-No, I'm honored.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:53.920
﻿Tomorrow is the battle between
﻿Nils Nielsen, Sei and Reiji.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:55.750
﻿We can't miss it.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:59.920
﻿That boy Nils hasn't shown us
﻿his true power yet.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:05.360
﻿The technique he used on Greco
﻿in the American final round.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:10.270
﻿Which do you think will win?

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.970
﻿That's obvious.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:14.940
﻿Whoever's feelings are strongest.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:22.280
﻿I know what choice I have to make.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:26.820
﻿The choice that gets me
﻿closer to my goal most quickly.

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:30.620
﻿I'm sorry to take your time.

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:34.020
﻿Mr. Iori. Mr. Reiji.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.190
﻿You can just call me Sei, Nils.

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:38.300
﻿Yeah, and just call me Reiji.

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:39.960
﻿Alright.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:43.530
﻿So what did you want from us?

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.540
﻿We have a battle tomorrow.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:50.040
﻿Wouldn't it be bad if someone sees us
﻿meeting at a place like this?

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.110
﻿Sei. Reiji.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:56.880
﻿Do you know the special properties
﻿of Plavsky particles?

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:57.980
﻿Huh?

00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:01.520
﻿I just know they're special particles
﻿that can move Gunpla.

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.420
﻿Do you know how they're made?

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.790
﻿I don't know...

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.790
﻿How would I know?

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:11.060
﻿Please recall it.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:12.100
﻿Recall?

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:13.800
﻿Yes.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.300
﻿According to my deduction,

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.740
﻿one of you knows
﻿the secret of the particles.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.170
Us﻿?

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:21.240
﻿Yes.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.510
﻿I don't expect you to
﻿recall right away.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:27.910
﻿But when you do, if you promise me
﻿that you'll tell me the secret...

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:31.850
﻿I'll withdraw from tomorrow's battle.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.790
﻿What did you just say?

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:38.290
﻿I said I'll let you win.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.260
﻿You...!

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:43.460
﻿Nils, are you serious?

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:44.290
﻿Of course.

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:48.930
﻿The reason I entered
﻿this championship was...

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:54.610
﻿to find PPSE's hidden method
﻿for generating Plavsky particles.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:58.140
﻿Th-That's why you entered
﻿the championship...?

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:01.450
﻿You want to win the championship.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:02.910
﻿It's a win-win.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:05.520
﻿I can't believe it.

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.550
﻿What's the point of winning like that?

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:14.260
﻿Everyone in the tournament works
﻿so hard to build and fight Gunpla.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:15.960
﻿Don't you know that!?

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:19.830
﻿I understand, but I can't relate to them.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:22.570
﻿It's a mere battle of toys.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:28.470
﻿The Plavsky particle could well have
﻿revolutionary applications in every field.

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:34.440
﻿If so, then revealing its secret
will lead to scientific advancement.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.850
﻿Do that somewhere else!

00:11:36.850 --> 00:11:38.820
﻿This arena is for Gunpla Battle!

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.750
﻿This is the best way to
﻿get closer to the heart of PPSE!

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:45.460
﻿Don't insult those who
﻿are fighting in earnest!

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:46.820
﻿I'm in earnest, too!

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:49.260
﻿Your earnestness is different from ours!

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:52.430
﻿Reiji.

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:55.600
﻿Sei, there's no need
﻿to talk to this guy.

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:59.700
﻿So is this negotiation over?

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.300
﻿You said your name is Nils.

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:06.480
﻿If you want something, win it yourself
﻿and don't beg someone else.

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:07.280
﻿Win it myself?

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.750
﻿It means exactly that.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:13.620
﻿If you win tomorrow's battle,
﻿we'll do whatever you say!

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:15.750
﻿Is that okay, Sei?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.620
﻿Yeah!

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:19.590
﻿I'll hold you to that.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.490
﻿I'm strong, you know.

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:27.930
﻿Sure, your Gunpla's strong, but...

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:32.870
﻿- We're going to win!
- ﻿We're going to win!

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:40.810
<i>﻿We now begin match three
﻿of the quarterfinals.</i>

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:48.350
﻿It looks like those
﻿two are fired up today.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.750
﻿We're definitely gonna win, Sei!

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:51.590
﻿Yeah!

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:54.460
<i>﻿Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:00.300
<i>﻿Field 11, Castle.</i>

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:04.200
﻿- Sei Iori.
- ﻿Reiji.

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.840
- ﻿Star Build Strike!
﻿- Let's go!

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:10.910
﻿Where is he, Sei?

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:12.110
﻿Over there!

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:13.640
﻿The castle tower!

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:39.070
﻿The beam was cut in half!

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:41.300
﻿Just as I thought,
﻿a rifle's no good against that.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:43.710
﻿Iori.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:46.010
﻿Not just the rifle.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.150
﻿The particle-absorbing shield, too.

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:53.080
﻿It's useless against the Sengoku Astray
﻿that has no beam weapons.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:57.250
﻿Just like you said, it's no use.

00:13:57.860 --> 00:13:58.990
﻿Seems so.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:00.490
﻿Then...

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.860
﻿Activating RG System!

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:13.740
﻿There's only one way!

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:15.440
<i>﻿I see.</i>

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:19.710
﻿That's not a wrong choice.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:20.580
﻿But...

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:23.810
<i>﻿No matter what you do,
﻿my victory's unshakeable!</i>

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:26.850
<i>﻿Sorry!</i>

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:33.760
﻿So fast!

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:48.310
<i>﻿Take this!</i>

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.040
<i>﻿Build Knuckle!</i>

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:06.420
﻿What!?

00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:10.360
<i>﻿The particle band transformed
﻿from the acceleration of its fist!</i>

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:14.160
<i>﻿Gotcha!</i>

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:27.710
﻿- Wh...!?
- ﻿What!?

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:37.290
﻿That technique's the one that beat Greco!

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.010
<i>﻿People call this...</i>

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:40.660
..."particle fa jin".

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:42.330
﻿Fa jin!?

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:45.460
﻿Mr. Ral, what's "fa jin"?

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.800
﻿It's the ultimate secret of
﻿the Chinese martial arts.

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:52.540
﻿By sending your own "chi" energy
﻿into the opponent's body,

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:54.170
﻿you can destroy them from within.

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:57.440
﻿A Gunpla used that technique?

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:02.110
﻿He probably used Plavsky particles
instead of chi.

00:16:03.010 --> 00:16:04.010
﻿That's odd.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:07.980
﻿He named his Gunpla "Sengoku"
﻿but he's using Chinese martial arts.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:13.860
﻿I told you that I'm strong.

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:18.030
﻿Don't get too excited.

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:21.300
﻿Wh-What!?

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:27.040
﻿The Build Knuckle reached him!

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:28.810
﻿Reiji, one more attack!

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:30.570
﻿Yeah!

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.010
﻿How dare you!

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:35.150
﻿Build Knuckle!

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.050
﻿Particle fa jin!

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:56.330
﻿No! Do it!

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.000
﻿Not yet!

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:00.400
<i>﻿Discontinued.</i>

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:03.570
﻿What happened.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:07.680
<i>﻿I would like to explain
﻿to our viewers that...</i>

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:11.720
<i>﻿the battle is temporarily suspended,
﻿as it's difficult to continue.</i>

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:16.790
<i>﻿After one minute for repairs,
﻿the battle will resume. Please stand by.</i>

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:22.490
﻿I'll work on the right arm.
﻿Reiji, can you do the left one?

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:23.360
﻿Of course!

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:34.800
﻿How dare you hurt
﻿my perfectly built Astray...!

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:37.710
﻿How dare you...!

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:39.540
﻿Iori!

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.080
﻿Keep it up!

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.320
﻿Nils!

00:17:49.820 --> 00:17:52.820
﻿Win for me!

00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:55.760
﻿Please shut up.

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:59.330
<i>﻿15 seconds until battle resumes.</i>

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:01.630
<i>﻿Restarting Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:08.510
﻿Sei, what're you doing!?

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:10.540
﻿Hurry!

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:13.640
﻿Sei!

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:17.750
﻿No, they'll be disqualified!

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:19.350
﻿Sei.

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:23.020
<i>﻿Resuming battle.</i>

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.020
﻿- They made it!
﻿- That's good!

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:31.900
<i>﻿I'll beat you this time...</i>

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:36.300
<i>﻿With my Sengoku Astray!</i>

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:38.600
﻿You're the one who'll get beaten!

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:40.800
﻿No, it's you guys.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.810
﻿The winner will be...

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:44.710
﻿Me!

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:46.880
- ﻿Us!
- ﻿Us!

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.650
﻿Maximum power output!

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:01.520
﻿Wh-What's this reaction...?

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:05.530
﻿The fa jin particles didn't get through?

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:12.170
﻿The right arm is
﻿covered with instant glue!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:16.410
﻿No wonder the particles
﻿couldn't get through.

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:18.880
﻿But in this state,
﻿its Build Knuckle can't—

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:20.340
<i>﻿It can!</i>

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:25.320
﻿By using the particles
﻿flowing through the Build Strike,

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:28.690
﻿our Gunpla can move!

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:31.650
<i>﻿What a nerve...!</i>

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.750
﻿Particle fa jin!

00:20:08.730 --> 00:20:10.660
<i>﻿This is the last attack!</i>

00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:15.270
﻿- RG...
- ﻿Build...

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:18.670
- ﻿Knuckle!

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:28.040
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:32.450
﻿They won!

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:34.550
﻿Yes!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:36.090
﻿They did it!

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:38.450
﻿Oh my. I'm impressed.

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:49.170
﻿Nice, Sei!

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:57.970
﻿The next time we battle,
﻿I'll definitely win!

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:03.710
﻿I thought you were going to
﻿bring up that particle thing again.

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:04.450
﻿Huh!?

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:09.320
﻿Were you so caught up in the battle
﻿that you forgot?

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:15.660
﻿So you like Gunpla, too.

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:19.930
﻿Well be your opponents anytime, Nils.

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:23.130
﻿But we're gonna win next time, too.

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:27.100
﻿Nils.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:30.210
﻿Sorry about yesterday
﻿I misunderstood you.

00:21:30.210 --> 00:21:32.210
﻿After battling with you, I get it now.

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:35.810
﻿If we can do anything for you,
﻿just tell us.

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:36.710
﻿See you.

00:21:40.420 --> 00:21:41.220
﻿Nils.

00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:45.520
﻿I'm sorry, Caroline.

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:47.160
﻿I lost.

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:49.560
﻿You were great out there.

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:50.130
﻿No.

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:53.530
﻿I was so caught up
﻿in solving the mystery,

00:21:53.530 --> 00:21:56.800
﻿that I didn't even understand myself.

00:21:57.700 --> 00:22:00.700
I like Gunpla.

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:04.810
﻿Don't worry.

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:11.710
﻿Yajima Trading will continue
﻿to give full support to you.

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:15.120
﻿Of course, so will I.

00:22:15.950 --> 00:22:17.620
﻿Because I'm your girlfriend.

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:58.630
﻿Fellini's quarterfinal has begun.

00:23:58.630 --> 00:24:00.600
﻿Reiji, that fighter is...!

00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:02.440
Next episode, "Aila's Betrayal".

00:24:02.440 --> 00:24:05.020
Tell us it's a lie, Miss Aina!
